# Template for deploy/api.env, the API's settings file — copy it beside this one, then fill it in.
# `api.env` is gitignored; keep real secrets out of this template. `Config::load`
# (crates/api/api_configuration/src/configuration/mod.rs) reads the process environment after
# loading the settings file best-effort (`TBD_API_ENV_FILE` when set, else deploy/api.env under the
# checkout root), so an exported shell var wins over anything written here.
#
# Only DATABASE_URL and JWT_SECRET hard-fail on boot when missing in development; outside
# development the Discord OAuth trio, UPLOAD_DIR, MAP_ASSETS_DIR and GLYPH_ASSETS_DIR are required
# too. A value that is SET but
# malformed also hard-fails for TBD_DB_POOL_*, TRUSTED_PROXIES, DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN, the runtime
# directories and EQUIPMENT_EXPORT_SOURCE_DIR. Everything else degrades quietly, which is why
# "required for which path" is called out per var below: an empty Discord var does not stop the
# API, it silently disables — or subtly changes — one path.
#
# WORKTREES: `api.env` is gitignored, so a fresh git worktree has none. Copy the main checkout's
# `deploy/api.env` into the worktree, or export TBD_API_ENV_FILE=<main checkout>/deploy/api.env,
# before `cargo xtask mk rust-api`.
#
# PATHS: a relative path set here resolves against the process working directory, which is
# crates/api/api_server/ when `cargo xtask mk rust-api` starts the API; the commented examples
# below are written for that base. Left unset in development, MAP_ASSETS_DIR, GLYPH_ASSETS_DIR,
# UPLOAD_DIR and EQUIPMENT_DATA_DIR default to folders of the checkout, found by walking up from
# the working directory to the repository root marker, so the API resolves them from any folder
# inside the checkout. Started outside a checkout, the API refuses to boot until each of those
# four is set.

# ─────────────────────────────── Server ───────────────────────────────
PORT=8080
# development | production. `development` additionally: exposes GET /api/v1/auth/dev-login, drops
# `; Secure` from the oauth_state cookie so the OAuth flow works over plain http, keeps blank
# Discord credentials legal, and fills the runtime-directory defaults below.
APP_ENV=development

# ────────────────────────── Frontend integration ──────────────────────
# SPA base URL. The OAuth + dev-login callbacks 302 here with the session in the URL *fragment*:
#   {FRONTEND_URL}/auth/callback#access_token=…&arma_linked=…&expires_at=…&refresh_token=…
# Use the SAME HOST STRING you browse the SPA on, and the same one as DISCORD_REDIRECT_URL below:
# `localhost` and `127.0.0.1` are different cookie hosts, and mixing them strands the oauth_state
# cookie → every login fails with #error=invalid_state. See
# documentation/runbooks/local_development.md §Discord OAuth2.
#
# The host that is free to move is this one: DISCORD_REDIRECT_URL has an EXTERNAL byte-exact
# contract (it must match a Redirect registered in the Discord Developer Portal, so changing it
# invalidates a working app registration), while FRONTEND_URL is read only by this API. In
# development `identity_and_access/handlers/oauth_host_guard.rs` refuses to start the flow when the
# two disagree.
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000
# CORS allow-list (comma-separated). Dev uses the Trunk proxy, so this matters in production.
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://127.0.0.1:3000,http://localhost:3000

# Leptos SPA served by the API (leave blank in dev — `cargo xtask mk leptos` / `trunk serve` owns
# the SPA on :3000):
#   - SPA_DIST_DIR: when set, the API serves the built Leptos SPA statically (COOP/COEP + SPA
#     fallback) AND /map-assets, so the app runs same-origin with the API (no separate web host).
#     At the flip, set it to the leptos dist and point FRONTEND_URL/ALLOWED_ORIGINS/the Discord app
#     redirect URI at the API's own origin (e.g. https://app.example.com) instead of :3000.
#   - MAP_ASSETS_DIR: the terrain dir served at /map-assets (in development, defaults to the
#     checkout's assets/terrains). Outside development it is REQUIRED and must be ABSOLUTE.
#   - GLYPH_ASSETS_DIR: the glyph dir served at /map-assets/glyphs (in development, defaults to
#     the checkout's assets/glyphs). Glyphs are shared by every terrain, so they sit beside the
#     terrain tree on disk; the two are joined under one URL prefix by the router. Outside
#     development it is REQUIRED and must be ABSOLUTE.
# SPA_DIST_DIR=../../frontend/shell/frontend_application/dist
# MAP_ASSETS_DIR=../../../assets/terrains
# GLYPH_ASSETS_DIR=../../../assets/glyphs

# ───────────────────────────── Runtime storage ────────────────────────
# What the API writes: CMS thumbnail uploads, served back at /uploads. In development it defaults
# to the checkout's gitignored assets/scratch/api/uploads, outside this crate; outside development
# it is REQUIRED and must be ABSOLUTE (the process working directory is a deployment detail, and the
# checkout is what the deploy rsyncs with --delete). The production unit points it at its systemd
# state directory (deploy/systemd/tbd-website-api.service); the staging compose file
# at a named volume. Leading or trailing whitespace is rejected at boot in every environment.
# UPLOAD_DIR=../../../assets/scratch/api/uploads
#
# The equipment datasets the import worker copies in from EQUIPMENT_EXPORT_SOURCE_DIR, with the
# indexes the development-only equipment data viewer routes read. In development it defaults to the
# checkout's gitignored assets/equipment; outside development, unset leaves the datasets
# unconfigured and a set value must be ABSOLUTE. The production unit points it at its systemd state
# directory too; the staging compose file leaves it unset. Leading or trailing whitespace is
# rejected at boot in every environment.
# EQUIPMENT_DATA_DIR=../../../assets/equipment
#
# On the deploy host, keep these four directories commented out: the unit loads this file as its
# EnvironmentFile, whose values override the unit's own Environment= lines, so a relative path set
# here would replace the unit's absolute one and stop the boot.

# ────────────────────────────── Database ──────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — the API refuses to boot without it (ConfigError::Missing).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://tbd:tbd@localhost:5434/tbd_reforger?sslmode=disable

# ── sqlx pool tuning ── all four optional. Unset or blank = the default shown (a ceiling of 25
# connections, 5 min idle timeout, 30 min max lifetime, 30 s acquire timeout). Whole numbers only;
# the ceiling must be ≥ 1. A value that is not one — `abc`, `5m`, `2.5`, `-1`, or `0` connections —
# REFUSES TO BOOT, naming the variable (ConfigError::MalformedValue via api_database::connect),
# unlike JWT_ACCESS_TTL_MIN, which silently falls back. Read at pool open by
# api_database::connection_pool::DbPoolConfig::from_env; `cargo xtask db test-it` sets none of
# them. Operators tune these without a rebuild.
# TBD_DB_POOL_MAX_CONNECTIONS=25
# TBD_DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECS=300
# TBD_DB_POOL_MAX_LIFETIME_SECS=1800
# TBD_DB_POOL_ACQUIRE_TIMEOUT_SECS=30

# ──────────────────────────────── Auth ────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — the API refuses to boot without it. Signs the JWT access token; changing it
# invalidates every issued session. Generate: openssl rand -base64 36
JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
JWT_ACCESS_TTL_MIN=15

# ───────────────────── Discord OAuth2 + role sync ─────────────────────
# Discord Developer Portal → your application. Full operator procedure — including how to tell
# the failure modes apart — is documentation/runbooks/local_development.md
# §Discord OAuth2 — live round-trip.
#
# Required for: signing in as a real Discord user, and for booting outside development at all.
# NOT required for `cargo xtask mk rust-api` to boot in development, and not required for
# dev-login — leave all of these blank and the platform still runs on dev-login.

# OAuth2 → General → Client ID (a numeric snowflake; 19 digits today).
# Blank ⇒ /auth/discord/login short-circuits to #error=oauth_unconfigured rather than bouncing
# the user to an opaque Discord error page (crates/api/api_discord/src/discord_client.rs).
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=

# OAuth2 → General → Client Secret (32 chars). Server-side only, used in the token exchange.
# Wrong or rotated ⇒ Discord 401s the exchange ⇒ the callback lands on #error=discord_unreachable —
# the SAME code a network outage gives, and the exchange error is not logged. Pre-flight the
# pair before blaming the network (no browser needed; 200 = good, 401 invalid_client = bad):
#   curl -su "$DISCORD_CLIENT_ID:$DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET" \
#     -d grant_type=client_credentials -d scope=identify https://discord.com/api/oauth2/token
DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Must be registered BYTE-EXACT under OAuth2 → Redirects in the portal — it is sent twice
# (authorize, then token exchange) and Discord string-compares both times. A mismatch fails at
# Discord's own consent screen, so you never reach the callback and see no app-side error.
#
# Its HOST must equal FRONTEND_URL's host. In dev the SPA on :3000 proxies /api to :8080, so the
# browser is on FRONTEND_URL's host when the flow starts and the host-only `oauth_state` cookie is
# scoped there; Discord then returns the browser to THIS host, and if the two differ the cookie is
# never sent → #error=invalid_state. Ports are irrelevant to cookies — :3000 vs :8080 is fine,
# `localhost` vs `127.0.0.1` is not. In DEVELOPMENT the API refuses to start the OAuth flow when
# they disagree (identity_and_access/handlers/oauth_host_guard.rs); in production it only warns,
# because a split-host deployment (SPA on app.example.com, API on api.example.com) is legitimate.
DISCORD_REDIRECT_URL=http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/discord/callback

# The guild whose roles decide the caller's web tier (Developer Mode on → right-click the server
# → Copy Server ID). Requested scopes are `identify guilds.members.read`
# (crates/api/api_discord/src/discord_client.rs).
# Blank ⇒ role sync is SKIPPED: the stored snapshot and the user's tier are left untouched, a
# tracing::error! is emitted, and an `auth.role_sync_skipped` WARN audit row is written — never a
# silent demotion of the whole community to enlisted. Setting this is necessary but not sufficient:
# the guild's role snowflakes must ALSO be mapped in seeds/discord_roles.sql, or every user
# resolves to enlisted on an otherwise perfect login.
DISCORD_GUILD_ID=

# Optional. Read only through Config::require_discord_bot_token; blank means "the bot is not
# configured" and every path that would need it reports that by name instead of sending an empty
# `Authorization: Bot` header. A set value that contains whitespace refuses to boot.
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=

# Channel webhook that announcements are pushed to as embeds
# (crates/api/api_discord/src/discord_webhook.rs). Independent of OAuth — it needs no client
# id/secret. Blank ⇒ pushing is disabled: the announcement still saves, and publishing records a
# CRIT audit row instead of posting.
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ─────────────────── Observability ────────────────────────────────────
# Operator bearer token for GET /metrics and the detailed GET /healthz
# (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`). Unset: /metrics answers 401 and /healthz serves only its
# public {status}. Game servers never use it: every game-server route takes the server's own
# machine credential (issued in Server Control).
OBSERVABILITY_TOKEN=

# ─────────────── Game-server process control ──────────────────────────
# Nothing to set here. Each game host runs the game server host agent
# (crates/fleet/game_server_host_agent), which
# polls the command ledger outbound over HTTPS with its own `host_agent` machine credential, and
# each game runtime authenticates with its own `mod_runtime` credential. Administrators issue both
# per server with POST /api/v1/servers/{id}/credentials; the API holds only their digests.

# ─────────────────── Background worker cadences ───────────────────────
# Seconds between the boot + interval republish of `server_statuses` to the live Server Intel SSE
# stream (crates/api/api_background_workers/src/server_status_publisher.rs). Ingest still
# publishes immediately on write. Default 10. Invalid / zero / negative → default.
# SERVER_STATUS_PUBLISH_INTERVAL_SECS=10

# Seconds between scheduled `leaderboard_totals` refreshes
# (crates/api/api_background_workers/src/leaderboard_refresher.rs). Default 900 (15 min).
# LEADERBOARD_REFRESH_INTERVAL_SECS=900

# Seconds between scheduled Discord → web role resyncs
# (crates/api/api_background_workers/src/discord_role_synchronizer.rs). Default 86400 (nightly).
# Invalid / zero / negative → default.
# ROLE_RESYNC_INTERVAL_SECS=86400

# ─────────────────────── Equipment data viewer ────────────────────────
# The Workbench equipment export's publication folder, which the import worker
# (crates/api/api_background_workers/src/equipment_export_watcher.rs) polls and copies into
# EQUIPMENT_DATA_DIR above.
# Blank ⇒ nothing is imported, and the viewer browses the datasets already imported. A set value
# must be absolute outside development; leading or trailing whitespace is rejected at boot.
EQUIPMENT_EXPORT_SOURCE_DIR=
